  "content": {
    "id": "p39-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "A chord splits a circle into two regions of area $a$ and $b$. The segment associated with the central angle $\\theta$ has area $a$, where $\\theta$ is measured in radians. Show that\n$$\\theta=\\sin\\theta+\\frac{2a\\pi}{a+b}.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\displaystyle \\theta=\\sin\\theta+\\frac{2a\\pi}{a+b}$.\n\nUse $a=\\tfrac12r^2(\\theta-\\sin\\theta)$ and $a+b=\\pi r^2$ to eliminate $r$.",
      "worked": "Let the circle have radius $r$. The segment area is the sector area minus the triangle area:\n$$\\begin{align*}a&=\\frac12r^2\\theta-\\frac12r^2\\sin\\theta\\\\a&=\\frac12r^2(\\theta-\\sin\\theta).\\end{align*}$$\nThe two regions together form the whole circle:\n$$\\begin{align*}a+b&=\\pi r^2\\\\r^2&=\\frac{a+b}{\\pi}.\\end{align*}$$\nSubstituting into the segment-area formula gives\n$$\\begin{align*}a&=\\frac{a+b}{2\\pi}(\\theta-\\sin\\theta)\\\\\\frac{2a\\pi}{a+b}&=\\theta-\\sin\\theta\\\\\\theta&=\\sin\\theta+\\frac{2a\\pi}{a+b}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 65
  },
